<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Špilberk Castle</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Spielberg Castle</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Špilberk Castle stands on a hill above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brno">Brno</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>. Founded in the thirteenth century as a royal castle, it withstood a Swedish siege in 1645, was rebuilt as a baroque fortress and from the eighteenth century served as a notorious <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> prison for political prisoners, including Italian patriots such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silvio-pellico">Silvio Pellico</a>. It is now the museum of the city of Brno.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spilberk-castle.jpg" alt="Špilberk Castle" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kirk · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C5%A0pilberk_(02).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
